 "source": "# MHA, GQA or MQA, at which learning rate? Six runs of a 12-layer Llama, in one file.\n#\n#   bux plan  examples/experiments/attention_ablation.bux\n#   bux train examples/experiments/attention_ablation.bux --only mqa\n#\n# The architecture and the recipe come from other files, by name. Definitions here\n# take the place of theirs everywhere, so llama3_8b's `block` picks up this `attn`.\nuse llama3_8b\nuse fineweb_wsd\n\n# Llama 3 8B, scaled down.\nd_model = 768\nffn.intermediate_size = 2048\nmodel = embed block^12 norm head(tied=true)\n\n# Three attentions, crossed with two learning rates: 3 \u00d7 2 runs.\nattn.num_heads    = 12\nattn.num_kv_heads = mha: 12 | gqa: 4 | mqa: 1\noptimizer.lr      = 1e-3 | 3e-3\n\nbudget = 3B\n",
